'''''Megapodius rokusi''''' is an extinct species of [[megapode]] from the Late Pleistocene [[Liang Bua]] of [[Flores]], Indonesia. It was described from a partial [[tarsometatarsus]] which derives from sediments dated to ''ca'' 190–120 thousand years ago. It was the largest species of the genus known so far, with an estimated body mass around 3.9 kg, which is slightly lighter than the contemporary extinct giant Australian megapodes like ''[[Progura]]''.<ref>{{Cite journal|last1=Meijer |first1=H. J. M. |last2=Sutikna |first2=T. |last3=Saptomo |first3=E. W. |last4=Tocheri |first4=M. W. |title=A new species of megapode (Galliformes: Megapodiidae) from the Pleistocene of Liang Bua, Flores |year=2026 |journal=Alcheringa: An Australasian Journal of Palaeontology |doi=10.1080/03115518.2026.2741158|doi-access=free }}</ref>

